{:edb/db-before-t 498 :edb/db-after-t 499 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533811 50 #inst "2026-10-05T02:36:01.775Z" 13194139533811 true] [17592186179748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252865 13194139533811 true] [17592186179748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252879 13194139533811 true] [17592186179748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252900 13194139533811 true] [17592186179748 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252907 13194139533811 true] [17592186179749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252872 13194139533811 true] [17592186179749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252886 13194139533811 true] [17592186179749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252893 13194139533811 true] [17592186179749 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252914 13194139533811 true] [17592186180167 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533811 true] [17592186180167 1145 "We start with the ratio $2:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of girls, and the denominator represents the number of boys.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $10$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{10}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $10$ girls and $5$ boys in the club. So the total number of members is \n\n$$\n10+5=15.\n$$" 13194139533811 true] [17592186180168 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533811 true] [17592186180168 1145 "We are given that the ratio of students who wear glasses to the total number of students is $\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students who wear glasses, and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{6}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $6$ students who wear glasses. \n\nSo the number of students who don't wear glasses is\n\n$$\n15-6=9.\n$$" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252866 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1089 "q-147065" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1100 "The ratio of yellow to white tulips in Mia's flower garden is $5:4.$\nIf Mia has $30$ yellow tulips, how many tulips are in the flower garden?" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1113 #uuid "981cb151-225b-5f7f-9223-5435f3713133" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252865 1145 "We start with the ratio $5:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{4}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow tulips, and the denominator represents the number of white tulips.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 6}{4\\times 6}=\\frac{30}{24}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  Mia has $30$ yellow and $24$ white tulips. So, the total number of tulips is \n\n$$\n30+24=54.\n$$" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252867 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252868 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252869 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252870 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252871 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1041 "selection" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252869 13194139533811 true] [17592186252866 1110 #uuid "031f89e7-6550-5618-8c6f-17718cd5a9b0" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252867 1034 "60" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252867 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533811 true] [17592186252867 1111 #uuid "191d936f-100a-528b-b3c8-96bc92975a93" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252868 1034 "48" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252868 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533811 true] [17592186252868 1111 #uuid "a571e587-f301-503e-8ce8-c664df5399ef" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252869 1034 "54" 13194139533811 true] [17592186252869 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533811 true] [17592186252869 1111 #uuid "e9fec51c